WEBVTT

00:00:33.784 --> 00:00:35.410
Good news, everyone.

00:00:35.494 --> 00:00:38.247
You all know the orphanarium
where Leela grew up.

00:00:38.330 --> 00:00:40.749
- Sure. We talk about it all the time.
- Really?

00:00:40.832 --> 00:00:42.125
No. Burn!

00:00:43.001 --> 00:00:44.419
Well done, fellows.

00:00:44.503 --> 00:00:49.049
Anyway, said orphanarium
has named Leela "Orphan of the Year."

00:00:49.132 --> 00:00:52.803
Your parents must be so proud.

00:00:52.886 --> 00:00:56.306
- Ooh, sorry.
- And the good news keeps on coming.

00:00:56.390 --> 00:00:59.184
Behold, my latest invention.

00:01:02.813 --> 00:01:04.857
Neat.

00:01:14.199 --> 00:01:16.743
Ta-da! It's a glow-in-the-dark nose

00:01:16.869 --> 00:01:19.997
you can wear over
your regular non-glowing nose.

00:01:20.080 --> 00:01:21.206
Observe.

00:01:23.125 --> 00:01:25.252
Whoa! Clool!

00:01:25.335 --> 00:01:27.713
Now I can punch you in the nose
in the dark.

00:01:30.215 --> 00:01:31.466
Where'd it go?

00:01:32.926 --> 00:01:36.430
Hey, Professor, what's all this groop
blurking out of the machine?

00:01:36.513 --> 00:01:39.933
That? It's, uh, nothing. Yes, nothing.

00:01:40.017 --> 00:01:42.686
If you think it's anything,
you're a suspicious moron.

00:01:43.395 --> 00:01:45.272
It looks like toxic waste.

00:01:45.355 --> 00:01:48.150
And it smells like toxic waste.

00:01:48.233 --> 00:01:49.484
What does it taste like?

00:01:50.861 --> 00:01:53.447
Delicious fig pudding! Ooh, that's good.

00:01:53.530 --> 00:01:56.283
But a distinct aftertaste of toxic waste.

00:01:56.366 --> 00:02:01.246
All right, all right! So the machine
produces a few toxic by-products.

00:02:01.330 --> 00:02:03.415
You don't have to make
a federal case out of it.

00:02:03.498 --> 00:02:05.834
I'm afraid I do.

00:02:05.918 --> 00:02:09.796
I order you to dispose of that toxic waste
properly or bribe me.

00:02:09.880 --> 00:02:11.632
Either way, it'll cost $500.

00:02:11.715 --> 00:02:14.927
Five hundred real dollars?
That's an outrage!

00:02:15.010 --> 00:02:20.015
Professor, I'll take care of that waste
for $499 and 100 cents.

00:02:20.098 --> 00:02:24.186
Hmm. I know that's a rip,
but I'll pay for the convenience.

00:02:24.269 --> 00:02:27.022
- Do you take credit cards?
- Let's find out.

00:02:29.900 --> 00:02:33.737
All right, environment.
You've met your match.

00:02:53.966 --> 00:02:57.135
Hey, get back in the sewer, weirdie.
No mutants on the surface.

00:02:57.219 --> 00:02:59.012
But he ruined my wedding dress.

00:02:59.096 --> 00:03:02.182
Honey, that thing was ruined
the minute it went on you.

00:03:02.266 --> 00:03:04.309
That's what I'm talkin' about.

00:03:07.604 --> 00:03:11.650
You know, it's not easy being an orphan.
Not if I have anything to do with it.

00:03:11.733 --> 00:03:14.111
Oh, God!

00:03:14.194 --> 00:03:18.532
But today's honoree, Turanga Leela,
has really made something of herself.

00:03:19.491 --> 00:03:22.202
I'll never forget the night
that cute little alien baby

00:03:22.286 --> 00:03:24.037
was abandoned on our doorstep.

00:03:24.121 --> 00:03:27.374
Because I have a photographic memory,
and I remember every night.

00:03:45.475 --> 00:03:48.937
What the... An alien language.

00:03:49.021 --> 00:03:50.480
I guess you're an alien.

00:03:50.564 --> 00:03:53.150
What a beautiful,
gigantic eye you have...

00:03:54.318 --> 00:03:55.819
Well, come on in.

00:03:58.363 --> 00:04:00.240
From those humble beginnings,

00:04:00.324 --> 00:04:03.869
Leela went on to become
a county certified starship captain.

00:04:03.952 --> 00:04:07.080
And so it is my pleasure today,
to nail her picture

00:04:07.164 --> 00:04:10.292
alongside those
of our most distinguished alumni.

00:04:18.634 --> 00:04:21.512
Thank you very much. Like many of you,

00:04:21.595 --> 00:04:23.472
- I never knew my parents.
- Give me a...

00:04:23.555 --> 00:04:24.681
I don't know...

00:04:24.765 --> 00:04:26.767
- ...if they were alien overlords...
- That little...

00:04:26.850 --> 00:04:29.019
...or simply underpaid alien janitors,

00:04:29.102 --> 00:04:31.313
- who fought crime on the side.
- There we are. Picture's up.

00:04:31.396 --> 00:04:33.524
It's crooked!

00:04:34.316 --> 00:04:37.945
In the end, though,
it doesn't matter who my parents were.

00:04:38.028 --> 00:04:42.616
All that matters is what I learned here,
within these unscalable walls,

00:04:42.699 --> 00:04:45.786
that I had the strength
to make it on my own.

00:04:45.869 --> 00:04:49.748
Just like all of you kids here today.

00:04:49.831 --> 00:04:53.085
Leela! Leela! Leela!

00:04:53.168 --> 00:04:55.337
Look at me! I'm Leela!

00:04:55.420 --> 00:04:57.506
Nuh-uh, 'cause I'm Double Leela.

00:04:57.589 --> 00:04:59.967
Whee!

00:05:00.926 --> 00:05:03.470
That's it, Albert.
No more espresso for you.

00:05:03.554 --> 00:05:06.348
Mind if we get a picture of you
with your picture for the news, ma'am?

00:05:06.431 --> 00:05:08.559
Yes. I mean, no.

00:05:08.642 --> 00:05:10.936
Just make sure you get my nonchalant side.

00:05:11.436 --> 00:05:13.522
Whoo!

00:05:26.952 --> 00:05:29.538
If those aren't tears of happiness,
please stop crying.

00:05:29.621 --> 00:05:32.124
It's okay, Fry. I'm fine.

00:05:32.749 --> 00:05:34.793
I won an award today.

00:05:34.877 --> 00:05:37.045
Is it this room that's making you sad?

00:05:37.129 --> 00:05:39.756
It's probably the room.
Come on. Let's go for a walk.

00:05:41.550 --> 00:05:43.635
I'm sorry you saw that, Fry.

00:05:43.719 --> 00:05:46.471
I usually try to keep my sadness
pent up inside,

00:05:46.555 --> 00:05:49.308
where it can fester quietly
as a mental illness.

00:05:49.391 --> 00:05:51.518
Yeah, I do that with my stupidness.

00:05:51.602 --> 00:05:55.814
I told a whole crowd today
that being an orphan made me strong.

00:05:55.898 --> 00:05:58.150
But all I really wanted was a mom and dad

00:05:58.233 --> 00:06:01.820
to hold me and stroke my hair
and tell me they love me.

00:06:01.904 --> 00:06:03.572
Then today's your lucky day,

00:06:03.655 --> 00:06:08.577
because I happen to be a holding,
stroking, lovin' machine, also spanking.

00:06:08.660 --> 00:06:11.079
That's not even close
to what I had in mind.

00:06:11.163 --> 00:06:14.082
Well, anyway, just remember
that people care about you.

00:06:14.166 --> 00:06:15.167
I know.

00:06:16.710 --> 00:06:18.754
Sometimes, when I'm lonely,

00:06:18.837 --> 00:06:21.131
I look up at the sky,
and I get this feeling

00:06:21.215 --> 00:06:25.844
that somewhere, on some unknown planet
circling a distant star,

00:06:25.928 --> 00:06:28.847
my parents are up there,
looking down on me.

00:06:45.322 --> 00:06:47.157
Yo, yo, Ba-zender, what up?

00:06:47.241 --> 00:06:49.284
My dumping business is booming.

00:06:49.368 --> 00:06:52.496
I just got hired to clean up
the set of Free Willy 3.

00:07:00.462 --> 00:07:02.089
Bender, cut it out!

00:07:02.172 --> 00:07:04.383
First of all,
the sewer mutants will be mad.

00:07:04.466 --> 00:07:07.344
Second, everything else that's
horribly wrong with what you're doing.

00:07:09.096 --> 00:07:11.890
Eh, those stupid mutants
can't do anything.

00:07:11.974 --> 00:07:14.643
You seem to be forgetting one simple fact.

00:07:14.726 --> 00:07:18.897
Namely, I'm up here,
and they are safely down...

00:07:32.828 --> 00:07:35.706
What did I do to deserve this?

00:07:35.789 --> 00:07:39.543
Behold, our once-beautiful
mutagenic sewage lake.

00:07:39.626 --> 00:07:41.753
The radioactive waste you've dumped in it

00:07:41.837 --> 00:07:44.923
has made it bright enough
to see how ugly we really are.

00:07:45.007 --> 00:07:46.842
Oh, man!

00:07:46.925 --> 00:07:49.386
As if our lives
weren't miserable enough already.

00:07:49.469 --> 00:07:52.723
- Tell me about it.
- Let the punishment commence!

00:07:52.806 --> 00:07:53.932
- Punishment?
- No fair!

00:07:54.016 --> 00:07:55.017
Bender's innocent!

00:07:55.100 --> 00:07:57.853
The instant you touch
these mutateous waters,

00:07:57.936 --> 00:08:00.063
your DNA will be forever altered,

00:08:00.147 --> 00:08:02.858
turning you into horrible mutants like us.

00:08:02.941 --> 00:08:04.651
- Especially him.
- Oh!

00:08:04.735 --> 00:08:06.987
Allow me to demonstrate.

00:08:15.412 --> 00:08:17.414
Ew!

00:08:17.497 --> 00:08:21.084
It's like that time
I peeked in the kitchen at Imperial Hunan.

00:08:21.168 --> 00:08:22.878
Submerge the prisoners!

00:08:26.507 --> 00:08:29.843
Wait. I don't even have DNA.
Why am I screaming?

00:08:29.927 --> 00:08:31.720
We're gonna beat you afterwards.

00:08:31.803 --> 00:08:35.057
Oh, God!

00:08:35.140 --> 00:08:37.976
Mutate! Mutate! Mutate!

00:08:38.060 --> 00:08:39.811
Turanga Leela!

00:08:39.895 --> 00:08:42.564
Who said that?
How do you know my real name?

00:08:46.068 --> 00:08:47.861
Whee!

00:08:52.783 --> 00:08:53.784
What happened?

00:08:53.867 --> 00:08:56.870
I don't know. I think I saved us somehow.

00:08:56.954 --> 00:09:00.541
Go after them!
The waters can't mutate us mutants!

00:09:10.509 --> 00:09:12.135
Duh, duh, duh!

00:09:13.971 --> 00:09:15.931
They went this way!

00:09:20.435 --> 00:09:21.770
Quick! In there!

00:09:26.942 --> 00:09:29.862
Kill! Kill! Kill!

00:09:29.945 --> 00:09:31.780
Kill! Kill! Kill!

00:09:37.578 --> 00:09:39.621
Great Cheech's ghost!

00:09:39.705 --> 00:09:41.039
What's this junk?

00:09:41.123 --> 00:09:42.124
It looks like...

00:09:42.833 --> 00:09:45.335
a timeline of my whole life.

00:09:45.419 --> 00:09:48.046
That's when we saved Earth
from a giant asteroid of garbage.

00:09:48.130 --> 00:09:51.300
And here's when I dropped out
and bummed around India for a while.

00:09:51.383 --> 00:09:54.386
And this is just last year
at Space Mardi Gras.

00:09:54.469 --> 00:09:59.057
It's like some kind of weird Leela museum.
And I'm the Leela.

00:09:59.141 --> 00:10:00.726
Dude, over here!

00:10:02.561 --> 00:10:06.064
It's all the best stuff
I ever flushed down the toilet.

00:10:06.148 --> 00:10:09.985
Those are some of my diary pages.
And my screenplay!

00:10:10.068 --> 00:10:13.780
And also, for some reason, the letter
I wrote you full of my personal feelings.

00:10:13.864 --> 00:10:15.657
Oh, I'm scared!

00:10:15.741 --> 00:10:20.162
My whole life has just been a show
for some perverted mutant.

00:10:20.704 --> 00:10:23.207
- They must be here.
- Capture them!

00:10:23.290 --> 00:10:24.666
And then, Bender ran.

00:10:25.083 --> 00:10:28.003
Leela, freak out later.
We're not done escaping yet.

00:10:32.925 --> 00:10:34.801
Got ya!

00:10:34.885 --> 00:10:37.763
- Take this!
- Ow!

00:10:38.222 --> 00:10:40.766
This time I'm calling
for the death penalty.

00:10:40.849 --> 00:10:43.936
And not just because I'm running
for reelection as supreme mutant.

00:10:44.019 --> 00:10:47.231
Four more years!
Four more years!

00:10:47.814 --> 00:10:49.441
Psst!

00:10:51.026 --> 00:10:53.487
Oh, very well. Your attention.

00:10:53.570 --> 00:10:55.656
Instead of being tortured to death,

00:10:55.739 --> 00:10:59.034
the prisoners shall hereby be expelled
from the sewers

00:10:59.117 --> 00:11:01.036
and never allowed to return.

00:11:01.119 --> 00:11:02.955
Oh, cruel fate!

00:11:03.038 --> 00:11:07.000
Can we really never return
to this dank pit of sewage?

00:11:07.084 --> 00:11:10.254
Wait a minute.
Why aren't you gonna kill us anymore?

00:11:10.337 --> 00:11:12.714
Yeah, what are you, chicken?

00:11:13.632 --> 00:11:17.010
Shut up, you two.
We can kill ourselves when we get home.

00:11:17.094 --> 00:11:19.555
They'll need transportation
to the surface.

00:11:19.638 --> 00:11:21.098
Bring in the airship.

00:11:22.850 --> 00:11:25.435
- Ew!
- We constructed it from the remnants

00:11:25.519 --> 00:11:28.522
of old discarded Macy's Parade balloons.

00:11:28.605 --> 00:11:32.860
Underdog's groin,
Bart Simpson's left ear and right shin,

00:11:32.943 --> 00:11:35.362
Garfield's owner Jon's forehead.

00:11:35.445 --> 00:11:37.072
Fire up the sewer gas!

00:11:52.254 --> 00:11:55.215
Move it, you ugly normals!

00:11:55.299 --> 00:11:57.509
Whoa!

00:11:59.011 --> 00:12:01.180
Huh?

00:12:01.263 --> 00:12:03.724
I'm getting dizzy. I can't walk straight.

00:12:14.651 --> 00:12:17.905
Whoa. Whoa!

00:12:25.245 --> 00:12:26.830
Come on, Leela. You can do it!

00:12:26.914 --> 00:12:28.790
Hurry, we're missing our bus!

00:12:40.511 --> 00:12:42.721
Hey, what are you doing?

00:12:42.804 --> 00:12:44.598
I'm gettin' on the bus!

00:12:45.390 --> 00:12:47.601
Don't worry. I'll be fine.

00:12:49.311 --> 00:12:50.771
They know something about me.

00:12:51.271 --> 00:12:53.148
And I've got to find out what.

00:13:23.262 --> 00:13:27.391
The lake didn't mutate me.
What is going on here?

00:13:27.474 --> 00:13:30.936
It worked for me. I used to be
a little blonde girl named Virginia.

00:13:35.190 --> 00:13:36.692
Who the hell are you?

00:13:36.775 --> 00:13:39.236
No one. And watch your language,
young lady!

00:13:44.825 --> 00:13:46.118
Stop right there!

00:13:46.201 --> 00:13:47.828
I don't wanna hurt you.

00:13:47.911 --> 00:13:50.497
I didn't want you
to hurt me either.

00:13:55.085 --> 00:13:57.296
Leela's going nuts, and I can't save her

00:13:57.379 --> 00:13:59.506
unless I learn more
about her mysterious past.

00:13:59.590 --> 00:14:01.466
Isn't there anything else you can tell me?

00:14:01.550 --> 00:14:04.011
Nah. Nothing that wouldn't be
a waste of your time.

00:14:04.094 --> 00:14:06.513
That's impossible,
because my time is worthless.

00:14:06.597 --> 00:14:08.432
Oh. Well, then there is one thing.

00:14:09.683 --> 00:14:12.603
It's the note I found with Leela
the day she was abandoned.

00:14:12.686 --> 00:14:15.981
But it's written in Alienese,
so no one on Earth can translate it.

00:14:16.523 --> 00:14:18.567
- Not even Brainzilla.
- Hand it over.

00:14:18.650 --> 00:14:19.651
Sure.

00:14:20.194 --> 00:14:22.029
I just wish I could be more helpful.

00:14:22.112 --> 00:14:24.239
Would you like some dirt
on any other orphans?

00:14:24.323 --> 00:14:27.910
Look. I'm trying to save someone here.
I'll have to come back for those later.

00:14:31.496 --> 00:14:33.332
- Can you translate it?
- Of course.

00:14:33.415 --> 00:14:35.459
But only into Beta-crypt-three.

00:14:35.542 --> 00:14:39.671
A language so complex, there's even
less chance of understanding it.

00:14:39.755 --> 00:14:42.132
I didn't ask for
a completely reasonable excuse.

00:14:42.216 --> 00:14:43.509
I asked you to get busy.

00:14:43.592 --> 00:14:45.469
Very well.

00:14:49.264 --> 00:14:51.141
Isn't that the same machine
that makes noses?

00:14:51.225 --> 00:14:53.393
It can do other things. Why shouldn't it?

00:14:57.314 --> 00:15:00.609
Of course, even if it is possible
to analyze the message,

00:15:00.692 --> 00:15:03.445
there's no way of knowing
how long it would take.

00:15:03.529 --> 00:15:07.449
It could take an hour,
or it could take a hundred million years.

00:15:07.533 --> 00:15:08.784
Is it done?

00:15:08.867 --> 00:15:11.912
Certainly not. Two dings means it's done.

00:15:13.163 --> 00:15:15.332
But not like that. Slightly more rapid.

00:15:31.056 --> 00:15:33.058
Where did they go?

00:15:37.896 --> 00:15:40.399
Good news, Leela. I landed the contract

00:15:40.482 --> 00:15:43.777
to empty all the spittoons
in Little Italy.

00:15:45.821 --> 00:15:46.822
Ew!

00:15:52.953 --> 00:15:54.830
That's it. It's done.

00:15:54.913 --> 00:15:58.292
I can't believe it. My mind is boggling.

00:15:58.375 --> 00:16:01.044
The analysis of the note
is printing out now.

00:16:26.111 --> 00:16:27.529
It's a girl.

00:16:27.613 --> 00:16:30.199
My God, she's beautiful.

00:16:30.282 --> 00:16:31.742
No extra anythings.

00:16:34.578 --> 00:16:35.996
What people skills!

00:16:36.496 --> 00:16:38.332
She's completely perfect!

00:16:38.415 --> 00:16:43.795
In my professional opinion as
an ear, ear, ear, nose and throat doctor,

00:16:43.879 --> 00:16:47.257
she is the least mutated mutant ever born.

00:16:47.341 --> 00:16:52.221
And yet, she's cursed to live
the horrible, degrading life of a mutant.

00:16:52.304 --> 00:16:54.681
Like all of us. Especially him.

00:16:54.765 --> 00:16:56.350
It's true.

00:16:56.767 --> 00:16:58.977
Maybe we can do better for her.

00:17:22.292 --> 00:17:26.630
I made this bracelet so that in some
small way, we'll always be with you.

00:17:27.047 --> 00:17:28.882
Even when it doesn't seem like it.

00:17:29.591 --> 00:17:32.803
During your entire life,
for example.

00:17:32.886 --> 00:17:35.556
You won't pass for human, cutie.

00:17:35.639 --> 00:17:39.935
But if my PhD in Excel-Linguistics
is worth diddly-poop,

00:17:40.018 --> 00:17:42.563
this note should convince them
you're an alien.

00:17:43.564 --> 00:17:46.567
And that'll be enough
to give you a real life.

00:18:00.706 --> 00:18:04.960
- She'll never know we're her parents.
- That's our gift to her.

00:18:05.252 --> 00:18:09.798
Better we should die than have her learn
the shameful truth of her origin.

00:18:09.882 --> 00:18:10.883
I'm with ya.

00:18:11.592 --> 00:18:13.177
I guess you're an alien.

00:18:13.302 --> 00:18:16.013
What a beautiful,
gigantic eye you have...

00:18:17.055 --> 00:18:18.473
Well, come on in.

00:18:40.621 --> 00:18:42.539
Keep quiet so she doesn't hear us.

00:18:42.623 --> 00:18:44.333
- What's there to talk about?
- Shh!

00:18:44.416 --> 00:18:45.834
Hands up!

00:18:45.918 --> 00:18:49.046
- Tentacles too!
- Don't say anything stupid, Morris.

00:18:49.129 --> 00:18:50.923
What is all this?

00:18:51.340 --> 00:18:52.633
Am I a game to you?

00:18:52.716 --> 00:18:55.511
Or some kind of
even more boring Truman Show?

00:18:55.969 --> 00:18:57.679
Do you believe I'm your Messiah?

00:18:57.763 --> 00:18:59.348
The mutant Dalai Lama?

00:18:59.431 --> 00:19:00.641
Stop me if I guess it.

00:19:00.724 --> 00:19:02.559
- Well, actually, they're...
- Morris, shh!

00:19:02.643 --> 00:19:04.561
And what about this?

00:19:09.066 --> 00:19:10.609
Where'd you get this bracelet?

00:19:10.692 --> 00:19:12.903
Did you steal it from me
when I was a baby?

00:19:12.986 --> 00:19:14.363
Or from my parents?

00:19:14.446 --> 00:19:17.032
You robbed my parents, didn't you?

00:19:17.616 --> 00:19:20.369
I bet you sick mutants killed them!

00:19:20.452 --> 00:19:25.415
My parents were confused aliens
lost on Earth, and you killed them!

00:19:25.499 --> 00:19:27.251
Is that it? Admit it!

00:19:28.460 --> 00:19:30.420
Yes, we killed them.

00:19:30.504 --> 00:19:32.130
You guessed the truth.

00:19:34.049 --> 00:19:37.386
Because of you,
I'll never know my parents!

00:19:37.469 --> 00:19:39.137
I'll kill you!

00:19:39.596 --> 00:19:41.181
That would be best.

00:19:50.107 --> 00:19:51.108
Stop!

00:19:51.733 --> 00:19:53.819
Thanks, Bender.

00:19:53.902 --> 00:19:55.028
Don't do it, Leela!

00:19:55.112 --> 00:19:57.823
- They killed my parents!
- Close.

00:20:01.869 --> 00:20:04.746
- They are my parents.
- Yes.

00:20:05.163 --> 00:20:08.458
I had the professor analyze the Alienese
letter that was found with you.

00:20:08.542 --> 00:20:10.544
- What does it say?
- I dunno.

00:20:10.627 --> 00:20:14.089
But the analysis showed
it was printed on recycled toilet paper.

00:20:14.173 --> 00:20:17.426
A squeezably soft paper
used mainly in the sewers.

00:20:18.552 --> 00:20:22.639
It says,
"Your parents love you very much."

00:20:22.723 --> 00:20:23.974
We still do.

00:20:24.057 --> 00:20:27.686
So, I'm not an alien? I'm a mutant?

00:20:27.769 --> 00:20:31.273
We never wanted you to know.
You deserved a better life.

00:20:31.773 --> 00:20:35.110
You must despise us.

00:20:35.194 --> 00:20:36.820
You're my parents!

00:20:37.279 --> 00:20:39.531
All I've ever wanted is to know you.

00:20:39.615 --> 00:20:44.036
This is the happiest moment
of my life.

00:20:51.585 --> 00:20:52.586
Aw!

00:20:59.384 --> 00:21:01.637
When I see you alone

00:21:01.720 --> 00:21:04.097
I see what's in your mind

00:21:04.181 --> 00:21:06.433
You want me
Yes, you do

00:21:06.517 --> 00:21:08.685
You don't need to tell me

00:21:08.769 --> 00:21:11.146
I know you love me most

00:21:11.230 --> 00:21:13.607
No one else take my place

00:21:13.690 --> 00:21:15.817
You need me
Yes, you do

00:21:15.901 --> 00:21:18.403
Forever and ever

00:21:19.363 --> 00:21:23.283
When we kiss
I see what's in your heart

00:21:23.367 --> 00:21:25.494
You love me
Yes, you do

00:21:25.577 --> 00:21:28.038
You don't need to tell me

00:21:28.121 --> 00:21:30.374
I know you love me most

00:21:30.457 --> 00:21:32.668
No one else take my place

00:21:32.751 --> 00:21:35.087
You need me, you do

00:21:35.170 --> 00:21:37.589
Forever and ever

00:21:38.632 --> 00:21:42.302
We are
Baby love child

00:21:43.095 --> 00:21:47.224
I'll take you so high
Groovy love child

00:21:48.141 --> 00:21:52.020
Give me a kiss
Baby love child

00:21:52.771 --> 00:21:54.565
Do it again